2026-11-22 13:47:06 - Agent_20261122134443 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 14 CodeQL results across the 3 queries in the virtualenv group.

TRUE POSITIVE (1):
- src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py:334-336 — `_request_context()` yields `ssl._create_unverified_context()` as a fallback for the PyPI metadata HTTPS request in `_pypi_get_distribution_info()`. Because the fallback silently retries without certificate validation, a network MITM can spoof PyPI JSON responses (release dates / versions) and steer which wheel versions periodic update selects and installs into environments; the query's CWE-295 is legitimate, though impact is limited because the download itself goes through pip with default verification. Filed as a true positive with a MITM scenario.

FALSE POSITIVES (12 of 13 remaining):
- src/virtualenv/discovery/py_info.py:73 — `__import__("venv")` is a constant literal probing for stdlib venv availability; not attacker-controlled.
- src/virtualenv/util/subprocess/__init__.py:8-17 — `run_cmd` is a list-based (shell=False) Popen wrapper with no user input; callers pass fixed interpreter paths.
- src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/acquire.py:52-74 — pip download invoked with an argv list; distribution/version_spec derive from virtualenv's own bundle config, not remote input.
- src/virtualenv/discovery/cached_py_info.py:127-138 — Popen of the interpreter path with fixed py_info.py script and random cookies; no shell.
- src/virtualenv/create/via_global_ref/builtin/cpython/mac_os.py:124 — `install_name_tool` called with argv list on local executable paths, plus in-process Mach-O patching; no shell interpretation.
- src/virtualenv/seed/wheels/periodic_update.py:203 — the `-c` code string is a dedent template formatted with the tool's own distribution/for_py_version/app_data values (repr-quoted), not remote data.
- src/virtualenv/seed/embed/pip_invoke.py:27 — Popen(argv) seeding pip, all elements built from local creator exe and bundled wheel metadata.
- src/virtualenv/seed/embed/via_app_data/pip_install/symlink.py:17 — `compileall` Popen with local image dir argv.
- tasks/make_zipapp.py:240, tasks/release.py:57, tasks/upgrade_wheels.py:23, tasks/upgrade_wheels.py:130-131 — maintainer-only build/release tooling (argv-list subprocess calls, fixed commands); no untrusted input, not part of the shipped runtime, so not exploitable.

No new independent vulnerabilities identified beyond the SSL fallback.
