2026-11-22 13:49:04 - Agent_20261122134443 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the single CodeQL result for py/virtualenv-zip-extract (Zip Slip) at src/virtualenv/app_data/via_disk_folder.py:77 and traced the underlying implementation.

Findings:
1. via_disk_folder.py:77 (AppDataDiskFolder.extract → virtualenv.util.zipapp.extract) — FALSE POSITIVE. The archive opened is `ROOT`, which is virtualenv's own zipapp (virtualenv/info.py: ROOT = realpath of the virtualenv package dir; IS_ZIPAPP checks os.path.isfile(ROOT)). The member is derived from `_get_path_within_zip(full_path)`, which abspath/realpath-resolves the requested internal path and raises RuntimeError unless it starts with `ROOT + os.sep`, so no caller-controlled member name can escape the archive. Additionally, zipapp.extract() rewrites `info.filename = dest.name` (a single path component produced by `root.path / path.name`) before calling `zip_file.extract(info, str(dest.parent))`, so even a crafted member name cannot introduce `../` traversal segments. The destination is virtualenv's own app-data cache dir (app_data.house / unzip/<version>), not an attacker-writable location.
2. src/virtualenv/seed/embed/via_app_data/pip_install/base.py:47-52 (build_image → zipfile.extractall) — reported as FALSE POSITIVE / lower risk: the wheel archive is the bundled or version-resolved embed wheel (`get_embed_wheel` / `discover_wheels` / periodic update), extracted into virtualenv's private image cache directory (`wheel/<py>/image/1/<name>`) via `zip_ref.extractall`; it is not reachable from any attacker-controlled archive in the zipapp path, and exploitation would require an attacker to control the wheel bundle/index itself, at which point arbitrary code execution is already implied. No CodeQL result pointed here; noted for completeness.

No confirmed exploitable path traversal was found; the flagged query is a build/bundling false positive.
